; The output stage. The lattice's output f in; the de-emphasis yd = f + 0.9 yd, then the sample 20 yd out as two
; values, the thousands and then the units (0-999), as lubdub's decoder outputs them. yd is kept as thousands H and
; units L with yd's sign; 0.9 L is (9 L + 5 away from zero) / 10. 2 yd is made first, its units summed on top of
; 2000 so they never go negative (STO keeps them as U, SFT 03 gives the carry); then 20 yd is 10 times that: its
; thousands are 10 T + U / 100 (SFT 10, SFT 02) and its units 10 (U mod 100) (SFT 21).
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            loop    INP   f        03-12: r = 0.9 L, rounded
  04                    CLA   lo
  05                    SFT   10
  06                    SUB   lo
  07                    TAC   neg
  08                    ADD   five
  09                    JMP   sh
  10            neg     SUB   five
  11            sh      SFT   01
  12                    STO   r
  13                    CLA   hi       13-21: yd = 900 H + r + f, into H and L
  14                    SFT   10
  15                    SUB   hi
  16                    SFT   20
  17                    ADD   r
  18                    ADD   f
  19                    STO   lo
  20                    SFT   03
  21                    STO   hi
  22                    CLA   two      22-42: 2 yd as T and U, then 20 yd
  23                    SFT   30
  24                    ADD   lo
  25                    ADD   lo
  26                    STO   u
  27                    SFT   03
  28                    ADD   hi
  29                    ADD   hi
  30                    SUB   two
  31                    SFT   10
  32                    STO   th
  33                    CLA   u
  34                    SFT   02
  35                    ADD   th
  36                    STO   th
  37                    CLA   u
  38                    SFT   21
  39                    STO   u
  40                    OUT   th
  41                    OUT   u
  42                    JMP   loop
  50            f       DATA  0
  51            lo      DATA  0
  52            hi      DATA  0
  53            r       DATA  0
  54            u       DATA  0
  55            th      DATA  0
  56            five    DATA  5
  57            two     DATA  2
